>                   Obviously, not picking things up is the way to go,
> but then you screw yourself over due to a lack of items. I guess, to be
> specific, what are some good ways to safekeep items without carrying
> them? 

The typical stash consists of chest or box on a square with a burned or
engraved E-word and possibly a cursed item. That way no monsters will eat
it or carry it away (except for exceptionally strong @s maybe?). Monsters
also don't open containers. As to choice of level, an altar is handy for
BUC-testing, and a branch level is advantegous because you'll be doing a
lot of trips to this level.

>       Or how does one determine what items are necessary, or at least
> what items are more important, when increasing one's load? 

Experience. Generally, I carry my main weapons and armor, some attack
wands, some food, a light source, and some emergency items (c?oT,
c!oGL,!oFH, /oT,/oD,/oF), as well as some attack wands and optional items. 
I do not carry spellbooks, potions, scrolls and rings that are not useful 
in a fight, gems, etc. Identifying, polypiling, item improvement and the
like are all done at the stash level.


